    w: 1, title: "The God of Justice and Mercy: Introduction to the Course", theme: "God is just and merciful, defends the vulnerable and calls his people to do justice, love kindness and walk humbly, so concern for the poor and oppressed is part of faithful discipleship",
    summary: "This opening lesson shows that justice and mercy flow from God's own character. Micah 6:8 summarises what the Lord requires. Psalm 146:5-9 praises the God who executes justice for the oppressed, gives food to the hungry, sets prisoners free and watches over the sojourners, the fatherless and the widow. Deuteronomy 10:17-19 shows that the Lord loves the sojourner. The lesson introduces the plan of the course and stresses that it is non-partisan and aims at shared biblical duty.",
