    apply: "Plan a fast that includes giving the money saved to someone in need. Review your church's or your own giving and service to the poor. Memorise Amos 5:24. Share your plan with a trusted friend or family member this week and ask them to check in with you, then thank God for any progress.",
    activity: "Read Amos 5:21-24 and Isaiah 58:3-10. Compare the false and true fast. Plan one practical act of justice or mercy for the class and pray.",
    takeHome: "Read Amos 5, Isaiah 1 and 58 and Micah 3. Write how your worship and service can be better integrated. Memorise Amos 5:24.",
    prayer: "Confess hypocrisy and neglect. Ask God to let justice roll down in our lives and communities.",
    teacher: "Teach the prophets' message with humility and avoid using it to attack particular groups or leaders. Link to practical projects. Be aware of learners who feel overwhelmed by injustice and provide hope and achievable steps.",
    assess: "Weekly check: ask learners to name one way worship and justice go together.",
    mcq1: ["What does Amos 5:24 say should roll down like waters?", ["Justice", "Gold", "Songs", "Sacrifices"], 0, "Justice."],
    mcq2: ["What does Isaiah 58:7 say to share with the hungry?", ["Your bread", "Your opinions", "Your tools", "Your fears"], 0, "Your bread."],
